### 1.5 Category Classification & Tier Routing

**Feature vector.** The Guardian classifier receives:
$$\psi_t = \bigl(\Delta_t,\; \Delta_{t-1},\; \Delta_{t-2},\; \nabla\Delta_t,\; B_t,\; \sin(2\pi h/24),\; \cos(2\pi h/24),\; \bar\Delta_{7d}\bigr)^\top \in \mathbb{R}^8$$
where $\nabla\Delta_t = \Delta_t - \Delta_{t-1}$, $h$ is current hour, and $\bar\Delta_{7d}$ is the 7-day rolling mean of $\Delta_t$.

**Classifier.** A five-class MLP $f_\phi: \mathbb{R}^8 \to \Delta^4$ with architecture [8 → 32 → 32 → 16 → 5], ReLU activations, and temperature-scaled softmax output (temperature $T_{cal}$ fit by minimizing NLL on held-out validation set via Platt scaling). Let $\hat{c}_t = \arg\max_c [f_\phi(\psi_t)]_c$ and calibrated confidence $\kappa_t = [f_\phi(\psi_t)]_{\hat{c}_t} / T_{cal}$. The label set is:

$$\mathcal{C} = \{\text{Nominal},\; \text{Forgotten},\; \text{Drift},\; \text{Risk},\; \text{Emergency}\}$$

**Trust-adaptive thresholds.** Thresholds $\tau_{soft}, \tau_{hard}$ are sigmoid-modulated by the current trust budget:
$$\tau_{soft}(B_t) = \tau^0_{soft} + \frac{\tau^1_{soft} - \tau^0_{soft}}{1 + e^{-\beta_\tau(B_t - B_{mid})}}$$
$$\tau_{hard}(B_t) = \tau^0_{hard} + \frac{\tau^1_{hard} - \tau^0_{hard}}{1 + e^{-\beta_\tau(B_t - B_{mid})}}$$
with $\tau^0 < \tau^1$ so that a depleted budget raises both thresholds (conservative mode) and a high budget lowers them (proactive mode).

**Tier routing — exhaustive and mutually exclusive.** The mapping $T: \mathcal{C} \times [0,1] \times [B_{min}, B_{max}] \to \{0,1,2,3,4\}$ is:

$$T(\hat{c}_t, \kappa_t, B_t) = \begin{cases}
0 & \hat{c}_t = \text{Nominal} \\
1 & \hat{c}_t \in \{\text{Forgotten}, \text{Drift}\} \;\land\; \kappa_t < \tau_{soft}(B_t) \\
2 & \hat{c}_t \in \{\text{Forgotten}, \text{Drift}\} \;\land\; \kappa_t \geq \tau_{soft}(B_t) \\
2 & \hat{c}_t \in \{\text{Risk}, \text{Opportunity}\} \;\land\; \kappa_t < \tau_{hard}(B_t) \\
3 & \hat{c}_t \in \{\text{Risk}, \text{Opportunity}\} \;\land\; \kappa_t \geq \tau_{hard}(B_t) \\
4 & \hat{c}_t = \text{Emergency}
\end{cases}$$

Tier 0 is silence. Tier 4 bypasses all soft blocks. The $\{\text{Risk}, \text{Opportunity}\}$ pairing at tiers 2–3 reflects asymmetric actionability: high-confidence opportunities escalate to proactive suggestions, not merely reminders.

