### 3.4 Cold-Start Protocol

**Phase 0 — Intake (day 0):** Profile questionnaire (age, chronotype, medication regimen, known conditions) → cluster assignment $k^* = \arg\max_k \pi_k P(\text{profile} \mid \mu_k)$. Parameters initialized: $\hat\theta_0 = \mu_{k^*}$, $\Sigma_0 = \Sigma_{k^*}$. Trust budget: $B_0 = B_{mid}$.

**Phase 1 — Silent observation (hours 0–72):** No interventions except Tier 4 emergency. Model observes, builds initial posterior $\hat\theta_{72h}$. KL baseline $\Delta_0 = \mathbb{E}[\Delta_t]$ estimated over this window and used to set adaptive thresholds.

**Phase 2 — Soft launch (days 4–14):** Tier 1–2 interventions only. FPR monitored; if $> 0.03$, thresholds auto-raised and cold-start period extended by 7 days.

**Phase 3 — Full activation (day 15+):** All tiers active. Thresholds fully modulated by $B_t$.

