## PART V — SECURITY, PRIVACY & COMPLIANCE

### 5.1 Cryptographic Architecture

**At rest:** AES-256-GCM with 96-bit random nonces; keys in hardware-backed keystore (iOS Secure Enclave / Android StrongBox Keymaster). Key derivation for export: PBKDF2-SHA256, 600,000 iterations, 128-bit random salt.

**In transit:** ECDH-P256 ephemeral key exchange per session, mutual TLS 1.3. Certificate pinning for server-side endpoints (leaf + intermediate). Federated payloads additionally encrypted end-to-end before entering the MPC protocol.

**Alert signing (Tier 3/4):** Alerts are ECDSA-P256 signed. Payload: $\{\texttt{timestamp},\; \texttt{tier},\; \texttt{category},\; \text{HMAC-SHA256}(\text{sensor\_summary})\}$. Designated contacts can verify authenticity without accessing raw sensor data.

**Audit log integrity:** SHA-256 hash chaining: $\texttt{block}_t = \text{SHA256}(\texttt{event}_t \,\|\, \texttt{block}_{t-1})$. Root hash exported periodically and signed for regulatory review. Tamper-evident by construction.

---

### 5.2 Differential Privacy Parameters

Noise calibration for operating point $(\epsilon_0 = 1.0, \delta_0 = 10^{-5})$-DP over $K = 52$ annual rounds (using RDP tightening from Section 2.3):

$$\sigma_{RDP} \approx \frac{\sqrt{K \alpha^*}}{\sqrt{2\epsilon_0}} = \frac{\sqrt{52 \cdot 15}}{\sqrt{2}} \approx 2.09$$

Operating deployment: $\sigma = 2.5$ (20% safety margin). Clipping norm: $C = 1.0$. Privacy budget consumed per round: $\approx 0.017\epsilon$; annual budget: $\approx 0.89\epsilon < \epsilon_0$. Annual accounting tracked server-side; round deactivated if cumulative $\epsilon \geq 0.95\epsilon_0$.

