## PART VII — ARCHITECTURE INVARIANTS SUMMARY

The following invariants are enforced by construction and validated by the formal guarantees above:

1. **Privacy by default.** No raw data leaves the device. Federated updates are DP-noised and MPC-aggregated before the server touches them. (§2.3, §5.2)

2. **Convergence.** On-device personalization converges at $\mathcal{O}(1/t)$ in MSE, with proximal regularization preventing catastrophic forgetting of population-level priors. (§2.1)

3. **FPR stability.** Trust budget is a positive-recurrent Markov chain when dismissal pressure exceeds reward pressure; FPR is bounded above by a computable function of the stationary budget. (§2.2)

4. **Exhaustive tier routing.** Every $(\hat{c}, \kappa, B)$ triple maps to exactly one intervention tier; no unhandled state exists. (§1.5)

5. **Graceful degradation.** GP fallback activates on ML failure without data loss or silent error. Atomic model rollback on validation failure. (§3.2, §3.3)

6. **Tamper evidence.** All interventions and corrections are cryptographically hash-chained and exportable for regulatory audit. (§5.1)

7. **Human override supremacy.** Trust budget mechanism ensures repeated dismissals structurally suppress future interventions — the system cannot override user agency. (§2.2, §1.5)

