APPENDIX F — VALIDATION AND TESTING PROTOCOLS

F.1 Synthetic Phenotype Library

A conditional VAE is trained on de‑identified real‑world behavioral sequences (N = 2 000). The latent space is semantically regularised with the four drift archetypes (gradual, acute, seasonal, noise). We generate 10 000 synthetic 90‑day trajectories with ground‑truth anomaly labels at 1‑minute resolution.

F.2 Property‑Based Testing with Hypothesis

Invariants verified per run ($10^6$ random seeds):

· Trust budget stays in $[B_{min}, B_{max}]$.
· Tier routing is total and deterministic; no unhandled combination.
· Timing optimiser never issues a notification during a hard block (sleep probability > 0.8 or driving).
· Emergency tier always schedules at $t_{now}$ regardless of cost.
· Personalised model loss (ELBO) monotonically decreases on average over the first 14 days.

